<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bordeaux</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Burdigala</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bordeaux is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garonne">Garonne</a> in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. As Burdigala it was founded by the Bituriges Vivisci and became the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallia-aquitania">Roman Aquitania</a>. It was the capital of the duchy of Aquitaine and was ruled by the English kings from 1154 to 1453, a period that built its wine trade with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. It remains the centre of the world's most famous wine region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bordeaux.jpg" alt="Bordeaux" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mariette · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bordeaux_Place_de_la_Bourse_de_nuit.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
